# ── ~/.config/punto/statusline.sh ────────────────────────────
# Copy to ~/.config/punto/statusline.sh. Never tracked, never overwritten by a
# pull, per machine — the same deal as machine.zsh.
#
# statusline-agnoster.sh sources this as the last thing before it closes the
# bar, so everything above is in scope: $input (the raw statusLine hook JSON),
# every colour in the palette, and $PREV_FG.
#
# The powerline contract is two lines. Print your segment starting with the
# previous segment's arrow, then set PREV_FG to your own background's foreground
# code, so the closing arrow matches whatever ended up last:
#
#     printf "${BG}${PREV_FG}${SEP}${TEXT} content "
#     PREV_FG="$FG"
#
# Skip the assignment and the bar closes in the wrong colour. Skip the whole
# thing — print nothing, set nothing — and the bar is exactly as it ships.
#
# The trap: this runs on EVERY render. Anything touching the network here stalls
# the bar for as long as it takes. Write to a cache file from a cron or a hook
# and read the file here.
#
# Getting it wrong is cheap, though. A syntax error aborts the source and the bar
# renders exactly as it ships; an `exit` ends the script there, costing the
# closing arrow and nothing else. Both measured. Return early with an `if` all
# the same — `exit` in a sourced file reads like a bug to whoever finds it next.
#
# In scope: $input, $PREV_FG, $SEP, $BLACK, $PAPER, $RESET, and every palette
# defined above the source point — the identity colours (statusline-agnoster.sh
# :24-41), the line-2 ladder BG_MODEL / BG_EFFORT / BG_CHERRY, and the ctx band
# pastels BG_LAVENDER / BG_SEAFOAM / BG_BUTTER / BG_SALMON with their FG_ twins.
#
# A ramp of your own is four hex triples and belongs here rather than in the
# repo. Keep every background light enough to take $BLACK, which is what every
# segment on this bar uses for ink.

# ── Spend, from a cache file ─────────────────────────────────
# Cost matters on a work machine and nowhere else, which is why it is here and
# not in the repo. The cache is written elsewhere; this only reads it, because
# anything reaching the network from this file stalls the bar on every render.
# BG_AMBER="\033[48;2;238;212;165m"; FG_AMBER="\033[38;2;238;212;165m"  # #eed4a5
# if [ -f "$HOME/.cache/claude-spend" ]; then
#     spend=$(cat "$HOME/.cache/claude-spend")
#     printf "${BG_AMBER}${PREV_FG}${SEP}${BLACK} \$%s " "$spend"
#     PREV_FG="$FG_AMBER"
# fi

