# ── Which account is logged in ───────────────────────────────
# A segment that says "work" on the work laptop and nothing anywhere else.
# printf "${BG_LAVENDER}${PREV_FG}${SEP}${BLACK} acme " ; PREV_FG="$FG_LAVENDER"

# ── The rate-limit gauges ────────────────────────────────────
# The 5-hour and 7-day windows used to be in the repo and are now here, because
# they are your plan and your usage rather than a terminal setting. If you want
# them, take them from this repo's history:
#
#     git show 4bec6ea:dotfiles/claude/.claude/statusline-agnoster.sh \
#       | sed -n '258,329p' >> ~/.config/punto/statusline.sh
#
# Line numbers rather than a pattern, because the block holds four `fi`s and any
# range ending at one stops two thirds of the way through. Delete the
# PREV_FG="$CTX_FG" line it carries — the repo sets that itself now.
